abstract: Yi guan lue shu [Brief account of a medical institution] is an 1871 Chinese
  hospital publication, catalogued with [Foochow] as its place of publication and
  柯為樑 (Dauphin William Osgood) credited with revision. Its Christian charitable purpose,
  hospital narrative, illustrations, donor lists and financial accounts support research
  on medical missions, local charitable networks and hospital publishing. Based on
  21 images of Bodleian Sinica 2017, the dataset provides TXT, JSON and TEI XML for
  37 designated physical faces, with uncertainties and source mappings. The provisional
  AI transcription includes selected source-image corrections; full human double collation
  and expert review have not been performed.
